Package: com.duoface.carplay.nativescenehost
Name: DuoFace Native Dashboard Scene Host (Development)
Version: 0.1.178~kbhud1
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Section: Development
Maintainer: DuoFace Independent
Depends: firmware (>= 16.0), mobilesubstrate
Description: QA178 kbdiag round 3 (private all-windows capture + 300ms late capture, behavior unchanged) and HUD exit hold (pre-hide snapshot handover). Previous QA177: app-touch recall, HUD exit handover, deeper keyboard diagnostics: controls recall now uses an app-side signal (QA176's scene-touch subscription proved dead on device: 0 hit-test lines in the exported log while in-pane taps demonstrably happened). The DF155 pilot relay (14 apps) and YouTube's own relay observe -[UIApplication sendEvent:] read-only (original implementation first, Began touches only, 250ms sender throttle) and report through the DF156 mailbox; Chrome recalls via noteUserActivity and logs qa177-recall on hidden-to-visible transitions; kill switch AppTouchRecall177 in the qa177 prefs plist (absent = on). Speed HUD exit handover: Chrome marks its lease Retiring and holds its HUD up to 4s until the CarPlay-process overlay announces its own HUD in its record (overlay-hud-visible), ending the exit blink; the overlay now file-logs every attach/detach with a reason into DuoFaceDockOwner.log. Keyboard diagnostics round 2 (still LOG-ONLY, no behaviour change): capture on DidShow with per-notification rate limits (QA176's shared 2s gate starved DidShow), plus keyboard window level, scene coordinate bounds and the host view frame/bounds/transform; Step-0 finding: a pane is a fixed logical-size scene (e.g. 414x736) scaled into place by a non-uniform transform, so the keyboard fault is that geometry contract (fix deferred). QA176 controls-recall/HUD-owner/keyboard-diagnostics: pane touches and Chrome's own windows again recall the logo + menus (the scene-touch subscription and the passive activity observer shipped unconnected in QA175; the 4s visible window is kept and activity handling is throttled against touch storms); speed HUD gets single-owner arbitration by lease priority (Chrome > DF144 standalone > native overlay163 — a presenter leases only while its HUD is actually visible, lower presenters hide and resume, none are removed; Step-0 census found exactly three presenters, all on the CarPlay display); hosted-app keyboard diagnostics are LOG-ONLY behind a flag (the app-side relay records keyboard window frame/screen, keyplane, input mode and hardware-keyboard facts, SpringBoard logs its surface frames beside them; no keyboard behaviour changes). QA175 touch reliability: pane-only root touch fall-through (QA173's version broke divider drags and leaked sheet taps), trailing-edge scene geometry commits with retry (was one-shot/per-pass in QA173), single-source divider visibility so the logo grip always returns, surface observers registered once after guards, GOFA shadow decoder moved to a serial queue (was racing on GOFA's thread); diagnostic build labels now name the current build (QA174 fix). Keeps the QA172 GOFA payload decoder in shadow mode (bubble speed stays GPS) and cuts diagnostic logging (de-duplicated, state-change-only, 256 KiB rotation), commits hosted-scene geometry in the same layout pass instead of deferring 0.30s, and adds a flag-gated root-window touch fall-through (default on) for hosted apps such as YouTube. Road speed limits/cameras/live route UNVERIFIED; QA162 GOFA-only Speed8 trial (no guessed road limit), plus QA161 scoped first SOLO remote geometry reference 120ms instead of 300ms, preserving media and split safety gates; retains QA160 read-only CarPlay Home trace. Native Home app-grid destination NOT fixed or physically tested. First-party experimental iOS16 rootless CarPlay Native12 integrated candidate with live app cards/recent, logo loading scene, touch activity borders, safer scene resize and foreground-only chrome. Real installed-app picker, source-owned external SBAppViewController host, two visible empty split panes with pass-through input, two clickable controls per pane, scene-ready/failure signals, split/swap/focus/drag and strict disconnect/heartbeat teardown. The CarPlay receiver draws no demo panes or fake action buttons; iPhone shows only actual installed-app inventory and active-session status. No external vendor binary or licensing; actual dual-app rendering and touch on iPhone X/CarPlay not yet device-verified. Opt-in 10-second physical disconnect per-process RunningBoard close with app PID provenance, reconnect cancel and phone foreground guard. Source-verified stage only; CarPlay native map tile/navigation and full iPhone auto-launch or screen-off are not device-verified. Unreleased QA candidate.
